1. GENERAL
In order to realize Women who are capable physically, mentally, spiritually, socially, in knowledge, and skills so that they are ready to be utilized, as well as efforts to protect Women and Children from all acts of Violence in order to achieve the goal of welfare through a Regional regulation that can serve as a reference for all parties related to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
The formulation of Regional regulations on Women's Empowerment and Child Protection has the purpose and objective as the implementation of the widest possible Regional autonomy, therefore the Women's Empowerment and Child Protection sector is one sector that is quite important to be managed and regulated in order to realize Women who are capable physically, mentally, spiritually, socially, in knowledge, and skills so that they are ready to be utilized, as well as efforts to protect Women and Children from all acts of Violence in order to achieve the goal of welfare through a draft Regional regulation that can serve as a reference for all parties related to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
The establishment of this Regional regulation is based on the principles of good legislation formation and the principles of material content of legislation.
The implementation of governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection aims to increase efforts for the Protection of Women's rights, fulfillment of Children's Rights and Special Protection for Children and to increase the role of Regional Government and the business sector, media and the Community in efforts for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection. The principal matters contained in the body of the Regional Regulation on the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Protection and Child Protection include:
a. Women's Empowerment;
b. Women's Protection;
c. Child Protection;
d. safe houses;
e. Women's Empowerment and Child Protection by Village government;
f. family quality;
g. cooperation; h. awards;
i. Community participation;
j. financing;
k. prohibitions;
1. investigation provisions; and
m. criminal provisions.

